@1 = ~Missing sister~
@2 = ~Local girl named Lessandra asked us to find a her sister named Kaya who went out of village to find a missing baby and has gone missing herself. She mentioned another commoner called Maralee have lost her child recently which prompted Kaya to start the investigation on her own.~
@3 = ~We met a thief in one of the huts within the village. He warned us not to side with Kaishas. Looks like she didn't win everyone over after all.~

// CotSC localisation batch 3: island dialogues; original journal @1-@3 retained.
@4 = ~You are... new. You need to speak to Kaishas. If she permits your stay, come back to me.~
@5 = ~My name is Lessandra. You are new around here and word has spread that you shall hunt the creatures down. If you are actually going north, I need your help. My sister, Kaya has gone missing. A couple moons ago Maralee's child was taken by the wolf-creatures. Kaya volunteered to find them.~
@6 = ~I tried to persuade her not to go, but she wouldn't listen. Please, find her.~
@7 = ~What does she look like?~
@8 = ~We don't have time for that, wench.~
@9 = ~We'll take a look, but won't promise anything.~
@10 = ~She has long, black hair and striking blue eyes. She wore a blue outfit the night she disappeared. She is a hunter, so surely she is okay but I just want her back.~
@11 = ~We don't have time for that, wench.~
@12 = ~We'll take a look, but won't promise anything.~
@13 = ~And I thought your kind is stoic. I should've never spoken to you. Walk away now!~
@14 = ~As long as you attempt I will be more calm. The island isn't big, you should be able to find her. I hope...~
@15 = ~I have nothing more to say to you!~
@16 = ~You're back. Did you find Kaya?~
@17 = ~Yes. But she's in a really bad state.~
@18 = ~No. Still looking.~
@19 = ~Kaya... she's bleeding badly. Thank you. I know what to do with her. I appreciate your help, stranger. I can tell there is kindness in the outside world. Maybe one day I shall see it. Here, take this as a reward.~
@20 = ~Keep searching, please. I can't lose my sister.~
@21 = ~Wha… hold it! I am not stealing anything. I'm just... looking around. Nice décor.~
@22 = ~Are you trying to rob this place?~
@23 = ~Yeah. Uneven ceiling and drafty door. Truly magnificent.~
@24 = ~Not to worry. We want to take some goods too. We won't tell if you don't.~
@25 = ~M... me? No! Of course not. Who do you think I am? A thief?~
@26 = ~Intentions are what counts, not the final representation of one's thoughts. Am I right? Heh, he.~
@27 = ~Oh, wait. You do not belong with Kaishas. You are her new goons aren't you? I shoulda guessed.~
@28 = ~Kaishas?~
@29 = ~And if so, then what?~
@30 = ~I am not messing around with you. Hand back what you've stolen.~
@31 = ~I do not like thieves. I think I shall deal with you right here.~
@32 = ~Then you and I are alike. You scared me there for a minute, friend. You shouldn't side with Kaishas or her tribe. They are... not who they say they are.~
@33 = ~I'll give you an advice, friend. Find yourself a cozy nest on the northern edge of the island, preferably nowhere near the shipwreck and live the rest of your life there. Hunt for food or go fishing and stick to your own place. You won't attract attention unless.~
@34 = ~Unless what?~
@35 = ~I spoke out of turn. Forgive me, my friend. I shall leave you in peace. Gotta find some more food before I go back to my place. Heh...~
@36 = ~Have you met her yet? The leader of this tribe. She mad and that is a fact. Anyway, I need some food so forgive me. Got a few more houses to rob. Must be off. Farewell~
@37 = ~I ought to give you a warning. Heed my wards. Kaishas is not to be trusted. You will never belong with her people. If anyone knows anything about her machinations, it is me. Now, excuse me. I must be off.~
@38 = ~Hah, brave one! I like your fire. You'll need all the courage to survive this island. You'll see what I mean.~
@39 = ~Then I shall put you down.~
